[size=4][color=#00ffff]OVERVIEW[/color][/size]
[b]Shadow Opportunist[/b] kicks in the moment you're caught sneaking, slowing time for everyone but you.


[size=4][color=#00ffff]HOW IT WORKS[/color][/size]
When you're sneaking and get detected during combat, time slows around you for a few seconds (3s by default).
You remain unaffected by the slow, allowing for swift repositioning, counterattacks, or escape.

You can use the effect as-is, with no perk requirements.
Or install the optional [b]New Perk Addon[/b], which adds:
[list]
[*]Shadow Opportunist (requires [i]Silence[/i] and 80 Sneak) - This version only activates if you've unlocked the perk.[/*]
[/list]


[size=4][color=#00ffff]COMPATIBILITY[/color][/size]
[list]
[*]The main file should be compatible with everything.[/*]
[*]The optional New Perk Addon has patches under Miscellaneous files.[/*]
[/list]


[size=4][color=#00ffff]CONFIGURATION[/color][/size]
A user INI is generated on first launch at:
[code]Data\MCM\Settings\ShadowOpportunist.ini[/code]
You can change the duration, perk requirements, visual and audio feedback, and player slow-time immunity here. Changes take effect after restarting the game.
Without the New Perk Addon, write required perks using local FormIDs without the load-order prefix, in [code]0x1234~Plugin.esp[/code] format, separated by commas. See [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/skyrimspecialedition/articles/6629]FormIDs and You[/url] for examples.
While the New Perk Addon is enabled, it always requires its own perk instead.


[size=4][color=#00ffff]UPDATING TO 2.0.0[/color][/size]
Before updating, leave combat and wait for the slow-time and visual effects to finish. Save and quit the game, then install the update.

Settings have moved from [code]Data\SKSE\Plugins\ShadowOpportunist.ini[/code] to the MCM settings folder shown above. Your old settings won't carry over. Configure the new INI after launching the game.


